method":"Residual income","low":0.787432,"point":0.830305,"high":0.876375,"weight":null,"formula":"Value = book + Σ (ROEₜ − kₑ) × Bookₜ₋₁ ÷ (1 + kₑ)ᵗ over 10 years; ROE fades linearly to kₑ; half of earnings retained","steps":["book $254.7M ($8.37/share), ROE -22.2%, kₑ 11.1%","= $0.83 per share; kₑ ±1 point: $0.79 – $0.88"],"inputs":[["Equity","$254.7M","Debt & rates module (app/debt.py, from the 10-K / 10-Q)"],["Net income, four quarters","−$56.62M","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, trailing four quarters: pretax income − income tax (the main site's reading)"]],"assumptions":[["Cost of equity","11.1%","CAPM build-up above"],["Fade","10 years to kₑ","fixed assumption"],["Retention","50%","fixed assumption"]],"source":null,"kind":"model","fit":"Equity is positive ($254.7M) and so is net income (−$56.62M), so the return it earns on book value can be compared with what shareholders require."},{"method":"Analysts' price targets","low":9.5,"point":9.75,"high":10.0,"weight":null,"formula":"Not a model of value: an outside or market figure shown for comparison","steps":["2 analysts, mean 9.75"],"inputs":[],"assumptions":[["Source","Yahoo Finance consensus targets (app/consensus.py)",""]],"source":null,"kind":"reference","fit":"Shown for comparison; not part of the stage-weighted value."},{"method":"52-week trading range","low":3.31,"point":null,"high":10.7,"weight":null,"formula":"Not a model of value: an outside or market figure shown for comparison","steps":["context, not a valuation"],"inputs":[],"assumptions":[["Source","daily closes",""]],"source":null,"kind":"reference","fit":"Shown for comparison; not part of the stage-weighted value."},{"method":"Path-to-margin DCF","low":13.3464,"point":42.5496,"high":71.6567,"weight":null,"formula":"The DCF with the EBIT margin moving in a straight line from today's to the peer median by year 5 (no dilution)","steps":["margin -2.9% → 8.0%; growth 10%, 9%, 7%, 6%, 4% → $42.55 (±5 points: $13.35 – $71.66)"],"inputs":[["Revenue","$1.69B","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, trailing four quarters (the main site's reading of the filings)"],["Operating income","−$48.58M","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, trailing four quarters (the main site's reading of the filings)"]],"assumptions":[["Target margin","8.0%","peer median operating margin"],["WACC","9.8%","build-up"]],"source":null,"kind":"model","fit":"It has an operating loss (−$48.58M) with revenue growth of 10%, so a DCF needs a path to profit — here to the peer median margin of 8.0% by year five."},{"method":"Path-to-margin DCF, dilution-adjusted","low":12.5857,"point":42.5496,"high":71.6567,"weight":0.25,"formula":"Value per share = equity value ÷ (shares + new shares); new shares = max(0, cash burned before break-even − cash today) ÷ price","steps":["Margin path: -2.9% today → 8.0% in year 5 (straight line); growth 10%, 9%, 7%, 6%, 4%","FCFF by year: −$13.38M, $25.79M, $67.73M, $113.9M, $162.7M; cash burned (negative years) = $13.38M","Funding gap = max(0, $13.38M − $23.25M) = $0 → 0 new shares at $9.34","Equity value = EV $1.35B − debt $82.40M + cash $23.25M = $1.29B","= $1.29B ÷ (30,414,000 + 0) = $42.55  (target margin ±5 points: $12.59 – $71.66)"],"inputs":[["Revenue, four quarters","$1.69B","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, trailing four quarters (the main site's reading of the filings)"],["Operating income","−$48.58M","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, trailing four quarters (the main site's reading of the filings)"],["Cash","$23.25M","SEC 10-K / 10-Q balance sheet (the main site's reading)"],["Diluted shares","30,414,000","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, diluted shares (the main site's reading)"]],"assumptions":[["Target operating margin","8.0%","peer median operating margin (SIC industry × size, base rates)"],["WACC","9.8%","the company's cost of capital (build-up above)"],["Terminal growth","2.5%","fixed assumption"],["New shares priced at","$9.34","today's price: an assumption — raising money in a downturn costs more"]],"source":null,"kind":"model","fit":"It has an operating loss (−$48.58M) with revenue growth of 10%, so a DCF needs a path to profit — here to the peer median margin of 8.0% by year five. Its losses must be funded, and the new shares that would take are counted."},{"method":"Exit-multiple (venture) method","low":26.0165,"point":39.5318,"high":55.5588,"weight":0.2,"formula":"Value per share = (revenue in year 5 × target margin × (1 − tax) × exit P/E) ÷ (1 + kₑ + stage premium)^5 ÷ diluted shares","steps":["Revenue in year 5 = $1.69B × (1 + 10%) × (1 + 9%) × (1 + 7%) × (1 + 6%) × (1 + 4%) = $2.38B","Net income in year 5 = $2.38B × 8.0% × (1 − 21%) = $150.5M","Equity value then = $150.5M × 16.9x = $2.54B","Today = $2.54B ÷ (1 + 11.1% + 5%)^5 ÷ 30,414,000 shares = $39.53","Range: P/E 12.3x at a hurdle 2.5 points higher → $26.02; P/E 21.2x at 2.5 points lower → $55.56"],"inputs":[["Revenue, four quarters","$1.69B","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, trailing four quarters (the main site's reading of the filings)"],["Tax rate","21%","tax ÷ pretax income (0–35%, else 21%)"],["Diluted shares (with the funding need)","30,414,000","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, diluted shares (the main site's reading)"]],"assumptions":[["Growth path","10%, 9%, 7%, 6%, 4%","its own growth fading to terminal (the DCF's path)"],["Target margin","8.0%","peer median operating margin"],["Exit P/E","12.3x / 16.9x / 21.2x","peer P/E, SIC 736 (Services-Help Supply Services), revenue $1–10B (136 observations)"],["Hurdle rate","16.1%","cost of equity 11.1% + 5% stage premium (an assumption)"]],"source":null,"kind":"model","fit":"It is not yet profitable (−$48.58M operating income, revenue growth 10%), so its value lies in what it can earn once it matures."},{"method":"EV/Sales vs Rule of 40 (all-company fit)","low":37.2163,"point":106.391,"high":297.758,"weight":0.15,"formula":"ln(EV/Sales) = a + b × (revenue growth + free-cash-flow margin); value per share = (fitted EV/Sales × revenue − net debt) ÷ shares","steps":["Rule of 40 = 10.2% growth + -2.0% FCF margin = 8.2","ln(EV/Sales) = 0.575 + 1.126 × 0.082 = 0.667 → EV/Sales 1.95x","= (1.95x × $1.69B − net debt $59.15M) ÷ 30,414,000 = $106.39; ±1 standard error (1.02 in logs): $37.22 – $297.76"],"inputs":[["Revenue, four quarters","$1.69B","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, trailing four quarters (the main site's reading of the filings)"],["Revenue growth","10.2%","last four quarters vs the four before"],["Free cash flow","−$33.30M","operating income × (1 − tax) + D&A − capex"],["Net debt","$59.15M","debt − cash + other claims"]],"assumptions":[["Fit","a = 0.575, b = 1.126, n = 1328, R² = 0.09","every covered non-financial company with revenue ≥ $50M, today"]],"source":null,"kind":"model","fit":"At the pre-profit / high growth stage, growth and cash generation drive the price: its Rule of 40 score is 8 (growth 10% + free-cash-flow margin -2%)."},{"method":"Survival-weighted value","low":12.4378,"point":41.7989,"high":70.3204,"weight":0.2,"formula":"Value per share = (1 − p) × going-concern value + p × liquidation value","steps":["p(fail within 5 years) = 1 − (1 − 0.4%)^5 = 2.0%","Liquidation value = max(0, tangible book $199.0M) × 80% ÷ 30,414,000 = $5.23","= (1 − 2.0%) × $42.55 + 2.0% × $5.23 = $41.80"],"inputs":[["Tangible book (equity − goodwill − intangibles)","$199.0M","SEC XBRL frames / debt module"],["Diluted shares","30,414,000","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, diluted shares (the main site's reading)"]],"assumptions":[["Going-concern value","$42.55","Path-to-margin DCF, dilution-adjusted"],["Failure probability","2.0%","one-year distress: the blended Merton / CDS / Altman / cushion estimate (credit panel)"],["Liquidation haircut","20% off tangible book","an assumption for a forced sale"]],"source":null,"kind":"model","fit":"It is burning cash (free cash flow −$33.30M a year, a runway of 0.7 years), so its value must allow for the chance it does not survive."},{"method":"Stage-weighted value (pre-profit / high growth)","low":18.9473,"point":49.9617,"high":95.5473,"weight":null,"formula":"Stage-weighted value = Σ weight × central value of the stage's methods (weights renormalized over the methods available)","steps":["25% × $42.55 (Path-to-margin DCF, dilution-adjusted) + 20% × $41.80 (Survival-weighted value) + 20% × $39.53 (Exit-multiple (venture) method) + 15% × $106.39 (EV/Sales vs Rule of 40 (all-company fit)) + 20% × $35.50 (EV/Sales vs peers) = $49.96"],"inputs":[],"assumptions":[["Weights","Pre-profit / high growth","fixed by stage before any result was seen (base_rates.STAGES)"]],"source":null,"kind":"blend","fit":"Its stage is “Pre-profit / high growth” — operating income ≤ 0, revenue growth +10.2% — which fixes these methods and their weights in advance."},{"method":"Combined forecast (3 months)","low":7.63455,"point":9.70746,"high":12.0267,"weight":null,"formula":"Not a model of value: an outside or market figure shown for comparison","steps":["3-month view; out of sample: error 15.7% vs 15.7% for 'no change', 80% range held 75% of the time (24,365 forecasts, 15 quarters)"],"inputs":[],"assumptions":[["Source","the Rotation / combined forecasts (forecast ledger, walk-forward)",""]],"source":null,"kind":"reference","fit":"Shown for comparison; not part of the stage-weighted value."},{"method":"EV/Sales fair multiple (multi-factor fit)","low":32.8032,"point":74.141,"high":164.656,"weight":null,"formula":"ln(EV/Sales) = a + b₁ × growth + b₂ × ln(operating margin, at least 0.5%) + b₃ × loss flag + b₄ × ln(revenue, $B) + sector effect;  value = (fitted EV/Sales × revenue − net debt) ÷ shares","steps":["= 1.801 + 1.016 × 0.102 + 0.561 × -5.298 + 1.272 × 1 + -0.086 × 0.525 + 0.156 (industrials) = 0.314","→ EV/Sales 1.37x; = (1.37x × $1.69B − net debt $59.15M) ÷ 30,414,000 = $74.14","±1 residual standard error (0.78 in logs): $32.80 – $164.66"],"inputs":[["Revenue, four quarters","$1.69B","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, trailing four quarters (the main site's reading of the filings)"],["Revenue growth","10.2%","last four quarters vs the four before"],["Operating margin","-2.9%","operating income ÷ revenue"],["Net debt","$59.15M","debt − cash + other claims"]],"assumptions":[["Fit","1328 companies, R² 0.47","every covered non-financial company with revenue ≥ $50M, today; ridge λ = 1"]],"source":null,"kind":"model","fit":"It is a non-financial company with revenue on file, so the multiple the market pays companies with its growth, margin, size and sector applies."},{"method":"Real option to expand","low":5.94106,"point":6.66499,"high":7.32122,"weight":null,"formula":"Value = (assets in place + C − net debt) ÷ shares;  C = S·N(d₁) − K·e^(−rT)·N(d₂), d₁ = [ln(S ÷ K) + (r + σ²/2)T] ÷ σ√T, d₂ = d₁ − σ√T","steps":["S = the expansion in year 5: the revenue it adds $689.8M (to $2.38B) × margin 8.0% × (1 − tax), as a growing perpetuity, discounted = $322.2M","K = capital to build it: $689.8M ÷ sales-to-capital 5.39 = $128.0M","σ = 80% (its stock, a year of daily closes), T = 5 years, r = 4.91% → C = $261.9M","assets in place = NOPAT −$38.38M ÷ WACC = $0; value = ($0 + $261.9M − net debt $59.15M) ÷ 30,414,000 = $6.66","σ ±25 points: $5.94 – $7.32"],"inputs":[["Revenue, four quarters","$1.69B","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, trailing four quarters (the main site's reading of the filings)"],["Operating income","−$48.58M","SEC 10-K / 10-Q, trailing four quarters (the main site's reading of the filings)"],["Stock volatility","80%","daily closes, last year (annualized)"]],"assumptions":[["Mature margin","8.0%","peer median operating margin"],["Growth path","10%, 9%, 7%, 6%, 4%","the DCF's"],["Volatility of the project","the stock's","an assumption: the business is riskier than the market sees only through its price"],["Return on new capital in perpetuity","15%","an assumption"],["Method","Black-Scholes (1973); real options: Myers (1977), Damodaran",""]],"source":null,"kind":"model","fit":"It is loss-making or growing fast: much of its value is the chance to become a larger, profitable business, which behaves like an option — worth more the more uncertain it is."}],"not_used":[{"method":"DCF — Monte Carlo 10th–90th percentile","why":"needs positive operating income (a cash-flow model on a loss only restates its assumptions); not used for banks, insurers or REITs"},{"method":"Regime-switching Monte Carlo 10th–90th","why":"needs the DCF and at least a few years of revenue history"},{"method":"Outside view — base-rate Monte Carlo","why":"needs the DCF and enough peer history"},{"method":"P/E vs peers","why":"needs positive EPS and six or more peers in its SIC group"},{"method":"EV/EBITDA vs peers","why":"needs positive EBITDA and six or more peers"},{"method":"Owner earnings capitalized","why":"needs positive owner earnings (net income + D&A − capex)"},{"method":"Shareholder yield (dividends + buybacks)","why":"pays no dividends and buys back no shares"},{"method":"Normalized (mid-cycle) P/E","why":"only for cyclical companies (industry or margin σ above 8 points)"},{"method":"Normalized (mid-cycle) DCF","why":"only for cyclical companies"},{"method":"Tangible book (asset value)","why":"only at the decline / turnaround and pre-revenue stages"},{"method":"Net cash (floor)","why":"only for pre-revenue companies"},{"method":"Sum of the parts (segments × peer EV/Sales)","why":"needs two or more reported segments"},{"method":"Graham number","why":"needs positive EPS and positive book value"},{"method":"Graham formula (revised)","why":"needs positive EPS, a growth estimate and the AAA yield"},{"method":"Net current asset value (net-net)","why":"current assets less all liabilities is negative (−$1.64 a share): no net-net value — normal for a company funded by long-term debt"},{"method":"Lynch fair P/E (PEGY)","why":"needs positive EPS and a growth estimate"},{"method":"Earnings power value (EPV)","why":"needs a positive normalized operating margin and the WACC (not for banks or insurers)"},{"method":"FCFE DCF (cash to shareholders)","why":"needs the DCF, positive net income and positive equity"},{"method":"H-model dividend discount","why":"pays no dividend (or its cost of equity is within a point of the terminal growth)"}],"stage":{"key":"pre_profit","label":"Pre-profit / high growth","why":"operating income ≤ 0, revenue growth +10.2%","rule":"operating income ≤ 0 over four quarters and revenue growth ≥ 10%","weights":[["Path-to-margin DCF, dilution-adjusted",0.25],["Survival-weighted value",0.2],["Exit-multiple (venture) method",0.2],["EV/Sales vs Rule of 40 (all-company fit)",0.15],["EV/Sales vs peers",0.2]]},"note":"Every figure above is from the company's SEC filings (XBRL frames, or the main site's reading of its 10-K/10-Q), the hub's daily prices, the debt module or the consensus module, as each line says; every assumption is fixed in the code before any result is seen. History and models, not investment advice."},"range":[0.787432,297.758]}